     PLDV (logic viewer) Help File             ESC Exits Help


          The Viewer Shows the Following States

          3 Logic Levels -- 1,0 and Unknown (three lines)

          Each Logic Level can be one of the Following

          Inputs    - GREEN
          Outputs   - LIGHT BLUE
          Tri-State - RED
          Pre-load  - DARK BLUE

          Buses are Shown in Red with the Hex Value Centered
          between the Transitions.


                                                       <CR> <more>
Mouse Functions 
----------------
Move Mouse Up       Move cursor up one position
                    If at top, move signals down
Move Mouse Down     Move cursor up down position
                    If at bottom, move signals up
Move Mouse Left     Move cursor left one position
                    If at side, move signals right
Move Mouse Right    Move cursor right one position
                    If at side, move signals left

Left Button         If highlighted and held drag signal
Left Button         If not highlighted, zoom in
Middle Button       If highlighted copy signal
Middle Button       If not highlighted, toggle reference marker
Right Button        If highlighted delete signal
Right Button        If not highlighted, zoom out

                                                       <CR> <more>
Key Pad functions 
------------------
Up arrow             Move cursor up one position
                     If at top, move signals down
Down arrow           Move cursor down one position
                     If at bottom, move signals up
Left arrow           Move cursor left one position
                     If at side, move signals right
Right arrow          Move cursor right one position
                     If at side, move signals left
^ Left arrow         Move cursor left half screen
                     If at side, move signals right
^ Right arrow        Move cursor right half screen
                     If at side, move signals left
Shift Left arrow     Move screen left one position
Shift Right arrow    Move screen right one position


                                                       <CR> <more>
Home           Move cursor to left side of screen
End            Move cursor to right side of screen
^ Home         Move cursor to begining of file
^ End          Move cursor to end of file
PgUp           Drag signal up one position, if highlighted
PgUp           Move cursor up ten positions, if not highlighted
               If at top, move signals down
PgDn           Drag signal down one position, if highlighted
PgDn           Move cursor down ten positions, if not highlighted
               If at bottom, move signals up
 +             Zoom in
 -             Zoom out
 *             Toggle reference marker
 r             Reset program to starting conditions
 ?             Display this file
INS            Copy signal, if highlighted
DEL            Delete signal, if highlighted
ESC or ^C      Exit program
                                                       <CR> <more>
Save Current File:   Shift F9

After editing the waveforms, you can save the current state by 
pressing Shift <F9>. The waveforms are saved in their current
arrangement using the first five characters of the original
filename with a new suffix of "-nn.HST". The value "nn" will 
be a number from 00 through 99 for any file already exists 
with the same name. The name of the saved file will be 
displayed in a small window for 3 seconds.


Undo Command:        F10

The undo command allows signal editing commands such as delete 
signal, move signal, and copy signal to be undone. The last 5 
edits can be undone. If the undo buffer is empty, a warning 
beep will sound if you press <F10>.

                                                       <CR> <more>
File Browser:        Shift F10

Pressing Shift <F10> opens a window and displays a file with the
same name (but different extension) as the file being viewed.  Up
to 8 files can be viewed sequentially.  Pressing <F10> again
moves to the next file until all files have been displayed.
Pressing Shift <F10> moves back to the previous file in the list.
Pressing the <TAB> key toggles between the waveforms and the
current file.  Pressing the <ESC> key exits to the waveform
viewer.

NOTES:

The current cursor position is at the top left of the screen.
The top right of the screen is for the delta readout, 
(i.e., the cursor position minus the reference marker position).


                                                       <CR> <more>
The reference marker is toggled on/off by the middle mouse button.
Both of these readouts change to red when zoomed out past one bit
of information per pixel.

The help screen can be exited at any time by pressing the ESC key
instead of paging through the whole file.

Page Up and Page Down can move though the help file.










